# Sandstorm Verge: "{T}: Add {C}." and "{3}, {T}: Target creature can't block this turn. Activate only as a sorcery." (CR 509.1b,
# 611.2a, 602.5d). Bot1's Verge, two Moxen and two Ornithopters come down on turn 1. Turn 2 Bot2 plays its Ornithopter, and the
# Verge cannot be activated on Bot2's turn (the window is not a sorcery's). Turn 3: with only two Moxen, both tapped, {3} is not
# paid (`Mana: short`); with the third Mox cast and tapped it is, exactly (the pool is empty right after) and targets Bot2's Ornithopter, which then
# cannot block Bot1's attacking Ornithopter. Turn 5: the same Ornithopter does block (the effect lasted that turn only), and
# the ability accepts Bot1's own Ornithopter as its target. Turn 6: Bot1's Ornithopter blocks Bot2's attacker (an effect on it
# from turn 5 is over). Turn 7: the Verge taps for {C} alone.

